const textVersion = {
  en: [
    "Every change to the pool joins a numbered transaction group (txg). Three txgs can be active at once, one in each state: open, quiescing, syncing.",
    "A write takes a hold on the open txg: txg_hold_open raises a counter of the CPU it runs on, for that txg. When the write is done, txg_rele_to_sync lowers it.",
    "The sync thread waits for one of three things: zfs_txg_timeout (5 seconds) since the last sync began, someone waiting for a sync (zpool sync, or txg_kick when the open txg holds more dirty data than zfs_dirty_data_sync_percent of zfs_dirty_data_max), or a txg already quiesced.",
    "It then asks the quiesce thread for the open txg. The quiesce thread closes it, opens the next txg at once so that writes never wait, and waits until every CPU’s counter of the closed txg is 0. It then hands the txg to the sync thread.",
    "The sync thread writes the txg in passes: the first writes the user data and the metadata above it; each pass allocates space, which changes space maps in the MOS, so it runs again until a pass leaves the MOS clean. Then vdev_config_sync writes the labels and the new uberblock: that one write commits the txg. A txg in which nothing changed writes nothing at all.",
    "Normally the next txg stays open while one syncs: the quiesce thread closes a txg only when someone asks. A caller that needs a new txg at once, such as dmu_free_long_range after a txg filled with frees, calls txg_wait_open, and then all three states are busy. There is never more than one txg per state.",
  ],
  fr: [
    "Chaque modification du pool entre dans un groupe de transactions numéroté (txg). Trois txg peuvent être actifs à la fois, un par état : ouvert, en clôture, en synchronisation.",
    "Une écriture prend une prise sur le txg ouvert : txg_hold_open incrémente un compteur du CPU sur lequel elle tourne, pour ce txg. Quand l’écriture est terminée, txg_rele_to_sync le décrémente.",
    "Le thread de synchronisation attend l’une de trois choses : zfs_txg_timeout (5 secondes) depuis le début de la dernière synchronisation, quelqu’un qui attend une synchronisation (zpool sync, ou txg_kick quand le txg ouvert contient plus de données modifiées que zfs_dirty_data_sync_percent de zfs_dirty_data_max), ou un txg déjà clos.",
    "Il demande alors le txg ouvert au thread de clôture. Celui-ci le ferme, ouvre aussitôt le txg suivant pour que les écritures n’attendent jamais, et attend que le compteur de chaque CPU pour le txg fermé soit à 0. Il remet alors le txg au thread de synchronisation.",
    "Le thread de synchronisation écrit le txg en passes : la première écrit les données et les métadonnées au-dessus d’elles ; chaque passe alloue de l’espace, ce qui modifie des space maps dans le MOS, et une nouvelle passe suit, jusqu’à ce qu’une passe laisse le MOS intact. vdev_config_sync écrit ensuite les labels et le nouvel uberblock : cette seule écriture valide le txg. Un txg où rien n’a changé n’écrit rien du tout.",
    "D’ordinaire, le txg suivant reste ouvert pendant qu’un autre se synchronise : le thread de clôture ne ferme un txg que si on le lui demande. Un appelant qui a besoin tout de suite d’un nouveau txg, comme dmu_free_long_range après un txg rempli de libérations, appelle txg_wait_open, et les trois états sont alors occupés. Il n’y a jamais plus d’un txg par état.",
  ].map(fr),
  es: [
    "Cada cambio en el pool entra en un grupo de transacciones (txg) numerado. Puede haber tres txg activos a la vez, uno en cada estado: abierto, en cierre, en sincronización.",
    "Una escritura retiene el txg abierto: txg_hold_open incrementa un contador de la CPU en la que se ejecuta, para ese txg. Cuando la escritura termina, txg_rele_to_sync lo decrementa.",
    "El hilo de sincronización espera una de tres cosas: que pasen zfs_txg_timeout (5 segundos) desde el comienzo de la última sincronización, que alguien espere una sincronización (zpool sync, o txg_kick cuando el txg abierto contiene más datos modificados que el zfs_dirty_data_sync_percent de zfs_dirty_data_max), o un txg ya cerrado.",
    "Después pide el txg abierto al hilo de cierre. El hilo de cierre lo cierra, abre de inmediato el txg siguiente para que las escrituras nunca esperen, y espera a que el contador de cada CPU para el txg cerrado sea 0. Entonces entrega el txg al hilo de sincronización.",
    "El hilo de sincronización escribe el txg en pasadas: la primera escribe los datos de usuario y los metadatos que hay por encima; cada pasada asigna espacio, lo que modifica space maps en el MOS, así que se repite hasta que una pasada deja el MOS limpio. Después vdev_config_sync escribe las etiquetas y el uberblock nuevo: esa única escritura confirma el txg. Un txg en el que nada ha cambiado no escribe nada en absoluto.",
    "Normalmente el txg siguiente sigue abierto mientras otro se sincroniza: el hilo de cierre solo cierra un txg cuando alguien lo pide. Un llamante que necesita un txg nuevo de inmediato, como dmu_free_long_range tras un txg lleno de liberaciones, llama a txg_wait_open, y entonces los tres estados están ocupados. Nunca hay más de un txg por estado.",
  ],
}[lang];
---

<figure class="txg" data-txg data-strings={JSON.stringify({ ...S, refs, consts })}>
  <div class="stages" role="img" aria-label={S.figure}>
    {
      (["open", "quiescing", "syncing"] as const).map((st) => (
        <section class={`stage stage--${st}`} data-stage={st}>
          <h3 class="stage-name">{S[st]}</h3>
          <p class="var">
            <code>{st === "open" ? "tx_open_txg" : st === "quiescing" ? "tx_quiescing_txg" : "tx_syncing_txg"}</code>
          </p>
          <div class="slot"></div>
        </section>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <noscript><p class="muted">{t.noScript}</p></noscript>
  <div class="live" hidden>
    <div class="disk">
      <span class="disk-label">{S.disk}</span>
      <span class="ub" data-ub></span>
    </div>
    <dl class="threads">
      <div><dt><code>{S.syncThread}</code></dt><dd data-sync-thread></dd><div class="timer" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
      <div><dt><code>{S.quiesceThread}</code></dt><dd data-quiesce-thread></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="buttons">
        <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" data-act="write">{S.write}</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="zsync"><code>{S.zsync}</code></button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="free">{S.free}</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="steady" aria-pressed="false">{S.steady}</button>
      </div>
      <div class="buttons">
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="play" aria-pressed="false">{S.play}</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="step">{S.step}</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="reset">{S.reset}</button>
        <p class="clock"><span data-clock></span> <span class="muted">· {S.clockNote}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="narration" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="log">
      <h4>{S.log}</h4>
      <ol reversed></ol>
    </div>
  </div>
  <details class="text-version">
    <summary>{t.textVersion}</summary>
    <ol>{textVersion.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ol>
  </details>
</figure>

<script>
  import { h, strings, fill, reducedMotion } from "../lib/svg";
  import { create, advance, step, write, zpoolSync, longFree, holds, timeLeft, CPUS, TXG_MASK, type Ev, type Model } from "../lib/txg";

  type S = Record<string, string> & { refs: Record<string, string>; consts: Record<string, number> };
  const RING = 32; // uberblock slots at ashift 12 (Hall room)

  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-txg]")) {
    const t = strings<S>(root);
    const q = <E extends Element = HTMLElement>(sel: string) => root.querySelector(sel) as E;
    const slot = (st: string) => q(`[data-stage="${st}"] .slot`);
    const btn = (a: string) => q<HTMLButtonElement>(`[data-act="${a}"]`);
    const narration = q(".narration");
    const log = q("ol[reversed]");
    const cards = new Map<number, HTMLElement>();
    let m: Model;
    let playing = false;
    let last = 0;
    let raf = 0;

    // A decimal comma in French and Spanish (D16.3).
    const fmt = (x: number) => (document.documentElement.lang === "en" ? x.toFixed(1) : x.toFixed(1).replace(".", ","));
    // Singular for 1, and for 0 in French.
    const one = (n: number) => n === 1 || (n === 0 && document.documentElement.lang === "fr");
    const text = (e: Ev) => (e.kind === "sync" && one(Number(e.n)) ? t.sync1 : t[e.kind]);
    const vars = (e: Ev) => ({
      ...t.consts,
      txg: e.txg,
      cpu: e.cpu ?? "",
      n: e.n ?? "",
      g: e.txg & TXG_MASK,
      next: e.txg + 1,
      prev: e.txg - 1,
      reuse: e.txg + 4,
      slot: e.txg % RING,
      ub: m.ub,
    });

    function card(txg: number): HTMLElement {
      let c = cards.get(txg);
      if (!c) {
        c = h("div", { class: "card" });
        cards.set(txg, c);
      }
      return c;
    }

    function cpuGrid(txg: number) {
      const g = txg & TXG_MASK;
      const cells = [];
      for (let c = 0; c < CPUS; c++) {
        const ws = m.writers.filter((w) => w.cpu === c && w.txg === txg);
        cells.push(
          h("li", { class: ws.length ? "busy" : undefined },
            h("span", { class: "c" }, fill(t.cpu, { c })),
            h("span", { class: "dots", "aria-hidden": "true" }, ...ws.map(() => h("i"))),
            h("span", { class: "n" }, String(m.count[c][g])),
          ),
        );
      }
      return h("div", { class: "holds" }, h("p", { class: "k" }, h("code", {}, fill(t.holds, { g }))), h("ul", {}, ...cells));
    }

    function render() {
      const placed = new Set<number>();
      const first = new Map<number, DOMRect>();
      for (const [txg, c] of cards) if (c.isConnected) first.set(txg, c.getBoundingClientRect());
      const put = (st: string, txg: number, ...kids: (Node | string)[]) => {
        const c = card(txg);
        c.className = `card card--${st}`;
        c.replaceChildren(h("p", { class: "num" }, `txg ${txg}`), ...kids);
        if (c.parentElement !== slot(st)) slot(st).replaceChildren(c);
        placed.add(txg);
      };
      // Open
      const d = m.dirty[m.open & TXG_MASK];
      put("open", m.open, cpuGrid(m.open),
        h("div", { class: "meter" },
          h("span", { class: "bar" }, h("span", { style: `width:${Math.min(100, (d / (t.consts.dsync * 2)) * 100)}%` }), h("span", { class: "mark", style: "left:50%" })),
          h("span", { class: "k" }, fill(one(d) ? t.dirty1 : t.dirty, { n: d }), " · ", fill(t.dirtyNote, { s: t.consts.dsync })),
        ));
      // Quiescing, or quiesced and waiting for the sync thread
      const qt = m.quiescing || m.quiesced;
      if (qt) {
        put("quiescing", qt, cpuGrid(qt),
          h("p", { class: "state" }, m.quiescing ? fill(one(holds(m, qt)) ? t.drain1 : t.drain, { n: holds(m, qt) }) : t.quiesced));
      } else slot("quiescing").replaceChildren(h("p", { class: "none" }, t.empty));
      // Once quiesced, the txg sits in tx_quiesced_txg and tx_quiescing_txg is 0 (txg.c L662-L663)
      q('[data-stage="quiescing"] .var code').textContent = m.quiesced ? "tx_quiesced_txg" : "tx_quiescing_txg";
      // Syncing
      const s = m.sync;
      if (s) {
        const rows = s.passes.map((b, i) =>
          h("li", { class: s.pass > i + 1 || s.phase !== "passes" ? "done" : s.pass === i + 1 ? "now" : undefined },
            h("span", { class: "k" }, fill(t.passLabel, { n: i + 1 })),
            h("span", { class: "bar" }, h("span", { style: `width:${Math.min(100, b * 8)}%` })),
            h("span", { class: "k" }, fill(one(b) ? t.passBlock : t.passBlocks, { n: b })),
          ),
        );
        if (s.noop) rows.splice(1);
        rows.push(h("li", { class: s.phase === "config" ? "now" : s.phase === "done" ? "done" : undefined },
          h("span", { class: "k cfg" }, s.noop ? t.noopCfg : t.config)));
        put("syncing", s.txg, h("ol", { class: "passes" }, ...rows));
      } else slot("syncing").replaceChildren(h("p", { class: "none" }, t.empty));
      for (const txg of [...cards.keys()]) if (!placed.has(txg)) cards.delete(txg);
      // FLIP: a txg card glides from one stage to the next.
      if (!reducedMotion())
        for (const [txg, c] of cards) {
          const a = first.get(txg);
          if (!a) continue;
          const b = c.getBoundingClientRect();
          const dx = a.left - b.left, dy = a.top - b.top;
          if (Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy) > 2)
            c.animate([{ transform: `translate(${dx}px, ${dy}px)` }, { transform: "none" }], { duration: 450, easing: "cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1)" });
        }
      status();
      q(".stages").setAttribute("aria-label", `${t.figure}. ${fill(t.aria, { open: m.open, q: qt ? `txg ${qt}` : t.empty, s: s ? `txg ${s.txg}` : t.empty, ub: m.ub })}`);
    }

    function status() {
      q("[data-ub]").textContent = fill(t.ubOnDisk, { txg: m.ub, slot: m.ub % RING });
      const left = timeLeft(m);
      q("[data-sync-thread]").textContent =
        m.syncState === "wait" ? fill(t.sWait, { left: fmt(left), timeout: t.consts.timeout })
          : m.syncState === "want" ? (m.quiesced ? fill(t.sTake, { txg: m.quiesced }) : fill(t.sWant, { txg: m.quiescing || m.open }))
            : fill(t.sSync, { txg: m.syncing });
      q<HTMLElement>(".timer span").style.width = m.syncState === "wait" ? `${(1 - left / t.consts.timeout) * 100}%` : "0";
      q("[data-quiesce-thread]").textContent =
        m.quiesceState === "drain" ? fill(t.qDrain, { txg: m.quiescing }) : m.quiesced ? fill(t.qWaitFull, { txg: m.quiesced }) : t.qWait;
      q("[data-clock]").textContent = fill(t.clock, { t: fmt(m.t) });
    }

    function tell(evs: Ev[], announce: boolean) {
      if (!evs.length) return;
      for (const e of evs) {
        const li = h("li", {}, h("span", { class: "at" }, `${fmt(e.t)} s`), " ", fill(text(e), vars(e)), " ", h("a", { href: t.refs[e.kind] }, `(${t.see})`));
        log.prepend(li);
      }
      while (log.children.length > 8) log.lastElementChild!.remove();
      // While playing, only stage changes are announced, so a screen reader is not flooded.
      const e = announce ? evs[evs.length - 1] : [...evs].reverse().find((x) => x.major);
      if (e) {
        narration.replaceChildren(fill(text(e), vars(e)), " ", h("a", { href: t.refs[e.kind] }, `(${t.see})`));
        if (e.kind === "uberblock") {
          const ub = q("[data-ub]");
          ub.classList.remove("flash");
          void ub.offsetWidth;
          ub.classList.add("flash");
        }
      }
    }

    function frame(now: number) {
      const dt = Math.min(0.25, (now - last) / 1000);
      last = now;
      const evs = advance(m, dt);
      if (evs.length) {
        tell(evs, false);
        render();
      } else status();
      raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function setPlaying(on: boolean) {
      playing = on;
      btn("play").setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(on));
      btn("play").textContent = on ? t.pause : t.play;
      cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
      if (on) {
        last = performance.now();
        raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
      }
    }

    const act = (f: () => Ev | Ev[]) => () => {
      const r = f();
      tell(Array.isArray(r) ? r : [r], true);
      render();
    };
    btn("write").addEventListener("click", act(() => write(m)));
    btn("zsync").addEventListener("click", act(() => zpoolSync(m)));
    btn("free").addEventListener("click", act(() => longFree(m)));
    btn("step").addEventListener("click", act(() => step(m)));
    btn("steady").addEventListener("click", () => {
      m.steady = m.steady ? 0 : 1;
      m.nextSteady = m.t + m.steady;
      btn("steady").setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(!!m.steady));
    });
    btn("play").addEventListener("click", () => setPlaying(!playing));
    btn("reset").addEventListener("click", init);
    // Off screen or in a background tab, the figure pauses.
    document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", () => document.hidden && playing && setPlaying(false));

    function init() {
      setPlaying(false);
      m = create(41);
      btn("steady").setAttribute("aria-pressed", "false");
      cards.clear();
      log.replaceChildren();
      write(m);
      write(m);
      m.log = [];
      narration.textContent = fill(t.idle, { open: m.open, synced: m.synced });
      render();
    }

    init();
    q(".live").hidden = false;
  }
</script>

<style>
  .txg {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
  }
  .stages {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .stage {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    min-height: 15.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .stage-name {
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .var {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .slot {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .slot :global(.none) {
    margin: auto;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .slot :global(.card) {
    flex: 1;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-content: start;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .slot :global(.card--open) {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .slot :global(.num) {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .slot :global(.k) {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .slot :global(.holds ul) {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }
  .slot :global(.holds li) {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: var(--space-1) 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .slot :global(.holds li.busy) {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .slot :global(.holds .c) {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .slot :global(.holds .n) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .slot :global(.dots) {
    display: flex;
    gap: 3px;
    min-height: 8px;
  }
  .slot :global(.dots i) {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    animation: drop var(--dur-2) var(--ease);
  }
  @keyframes drop {
    from {
      transform: translateY(-8px);
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }
  .slot :global(.meter) {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }
  .slot :global(.bar) {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--line);
    border-radius: 3px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .slot :global(.bar > span:first-child) {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--accent);
    transition: width var(--dur-2) var(--ease);
  }
  .slot :global(.bar .mark) {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--fg);
  }
  .slot :global(.state) {
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }
  .slot :global(.passes) {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .slot :global(.passes li) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4.2rem 1fr 4rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    opacity: 0.45;
  }
  .slot :global(.passes li.now),
  .slot :global(.passes li.done) {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .slot :global(.passes li.now .k) {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .slot :global(.passes .cfg) {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .live[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .disk {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .disk-label {
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .ub {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    padding: 0 var(--space-2);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .ub:global(.flash) {
      animation: flash 1.2s var(--ease);
    }
  }
  @keyframes flash {
    from {
      background: var(--accent);
      color: var(--bg);
    }
  }
  .threads {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .threads > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .threads dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .timer {
    grid-column: 2;
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--line);
    border-radius: 2px;
    max-width: 24rem;
  }
  .timer span {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .controls {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .btn code {
    font-size: 0.95em;
  }
  .clock {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .narration {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    min-height: 5em;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .log {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .log h4 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .log ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .log :global(li:first-child) {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .log :global(.at) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .text-version {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .text-version summary {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }
  .text-version ol {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .stages {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .stage {
      min-height: 0;
    }
    .threads > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .timer {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
